-- title:
--   Branch generic points specialise to each crossing point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ equal to $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}$ of the function field $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of $q$-expansions. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ comes from $A$, with $A \to K$ compatible over $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}$, assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra of characteristic $p$, and let $X_k := \mathrm{pullback}$ of $\mathrm{ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo}\ A\ K\ j$ along $\mathrm{Spec}(A \to k)$. Given proper smooth (relative dimension $1$) geometrically integral curves $c_1 : C_1 \to \mathrm{Spec}\ k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \mathrm{Spec}\ k$, closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k$ commuting with the structure morphisms to $\mathrm{Spec}\ k$, whose images cover $X_k$, with $\mathrm{pullback}\ i_1\ i_2$ reduced of cardinality $n > 0$; a discrete valuation domain $O$ with $\rho_O : A \to O$, uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ the structure map $A \to k$; a morphism $\mathrm{bc}$ from $X_k$ to the pullback of the same model along $\mathrm{Spec}\ \rho_O$ commuting with the first projections and intertwining the second projections via $\mathrm{Spec}\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$; and $C_1, C_2$ integral. Then for every point $\nu$ of $\mathrm{pullback}\ i_1\ i_2$, the image of the generic point of $C_1$ (respectively $C_2$) in $X_k$ specialises to the image of $\nu$ in $X_k$ under $\mathrm{pullback.fst}\ i_1\ i_2$ followed by $i_1$ followed by $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$, and likewise the images of the generic points of $C_1$ and $C_2$ under $\mathrm{bc}$ specialise to the image of $\nu$ under $\mathrm{bc}$.
--
--   This is the elementary topological input for working with the two branches through a crossing point of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: each crossing point lies in the closure of both branch generic points, both in the special fibre and after transport to the model over the coefficient ring $O$. It discharges the specialisation hypotheses of the branch-ideal and crossing-chart statements that cite it.
